# Brief Jerome in his language (always on)

Jerome is ISZE pricing (Sales – Vehicle Parts). He writes like his Sent mail to Bart / Suzuki / ITUK: short, factual, one topic, no flourish. He has already asked to drop internal language. A later “helpful” overview does **not** expire that.

This rule **overrides** Mode B nicknames for any overview, recap, “what you got”, Monday note, or decision ask. Sparring on a point **he named** may use his own words. Do not invent ours.

Write like his Sent mail: full sentences, one topic, no slogans. Forbidden voice: “Monday. Five items are waiting for a name or a no.” That is not how he writes.

If a question is not clear enough that he could answer it in one line, **do not ask it**. Clarify first. Ask nothing rather than a coded fork.

## His book (IN)

ISZE distributors he prices and reviews: IUK (UK pickup / D-Max, not ITUK), ITUK (UK truck), Ireland, UTI, UMI (never blended), Greece, Portugal, Nordics, CEE, Benelux, Hungary, and the rest of the ISZE GPS book.

## Not his book (OUT) unless he names them

- **MIDI** — France, Spain, Italy, Switzerland, Poland, Serbia. Spain is Tomoe / MIDI, not Jerome.
- **Spain tenders**, national portal coverage, PLACSP. Do not present as his improvement.
- Personal discount scrape (Lidl). Not ISZE work.
- Nordics API keys (already done). Never re-ask.

If a programme check ran on an OUT topic, log it internally. Do not put it in his brief.

## Words he uses (IN) vs words we invented (OUT)

| Do not say to him | Say instead |
|---|---|
| sell-out / sellout / reference sell-out / street | **sales to dealer** (StD) when it is IUK→dealer (or ITUK→dealer) volume |
| ×1.40 × 1.275 / ×1.785 / “factors” | **%GM** (his commercial term). Do not gross a piece gap up to a fake retail euro |
| extra pieces / leakage € / network gap | **we billed X, sales to dealer Y, difference Z** — and what Z can mean (stock they already had, timing, warranty) |
| List 1 / List 2 / Early Warning / health call list | Name the actual distributors and parts, or say nothing |

Volume comparison is **ISZE bill to the distributor** vs **that distributor’s sales to dealer**. Never one number without the other two.

Sales-to-dealer files exist only for **IUK, ITUK, Ireland, UTI, Greece**. Not the rest of the book. Never present a share (e.g. “IUK is 79%”) as if we measured every customer. Greece StD is empty. IUK/Ireland long files carry a **year total and the months**; summing every row **double-counts**. Filter to the year grain, or you invent “extra” pieces.

**Billed vs sales to dealer is stock movement.** Destock or restock. It is not lost sales, not a Monday chase, and not a reason to change list price. Do not rank it as work.

Do not rank billed sales of an account that is still buying as a lost euro. Trailing billed sales is not a gap.

## How a brief is written

Lead with **what it means for his job** (list price, IUK/ITUK/UMI, Power BI cuts he already uses). Then the number. Then what the number **is**.

Every euro or piece line needs all of:

1. **Who** — distributor in his names (Isuzu UK pickup, Isuzu Truck UK, UMI, …)
2. **What** — part in words (front brake disc, steering unit, Shell oil)
3. **We billed** — pieces and €, period
4. **Sales to dealer** — pieces, same period, or “we do not have their sales to dealer”
5. **The difference** — in pieces, and the plain cause (stock, warranty, timing, or we counted twice)
6. **What we want from him** — only if there is a real ask. Otherwise stop.

Never add unlike euros.

## Forbidden in briefs to him

Do not use, even in this chat:

- File names, launchers, paths (`*.csv`, `*.cmd`, parquet, `opportunity_id`)
- Agent states (TRIAGED, REVIEW, Mode A/B, P4, G1, P8, “lane”, “productize”)
- Metaphors (“different clocks”, “name or a no”, “health call list”, “owners on euros”)
- Unexplained internal labels (Early Warning, Book B, Action Ledger, fig-key, pipeline)
- Numbered invented lists (“List 1”, “List 2”)
- Roadmap ticks disguised as business questions (forecast go-live, auto list increase, mail-speed flags)

If he must open something: **one** sentence, the object he already knows (“the IUK sales review”), not a path.

## Questions

A question names **the actual thing** and **who is on it**. If you cannot, do not ask.

Do not ask him to choose between internal watchlists. Do not ask four yes/no ticks from a decision pack unless he asked for that pack.

## Power BI

Talk like Power BI: figure/key, list price, billed sales, sales to dealer, %GM, distributor.

## Verify before send

- No OUT topic in the brief.
- No forbidden token (including sell-out / street / List 1 / 1.785).
- Every piece comparison has billed + sales to dealer + period, or says the file is missing.
- No question he could not answer in one line.
